{
  "slug": "tdd-guard",
  "name": "Tdd Guard",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Enforces Test-Driven Development by intercepting file operations in Claude Code. When Claude attempts to edit or write files, TDD Guard validates the changes against TDD principles — blocking operations that skip tests or over-implement, and explaining what needs to happen instead.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill** and **3 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `setup` (Set up or update TDD Guard for the current project)\n- **Hooks** (3): `PreToolUse`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `SessionStart`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install tdd-guard@claude-community` from `nizos/tdd-guard` (`plugin`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "hook": 3
  },
